# PRIVATE INPUT TEMPLATE: safe to commit because it contains no actual secret.
# For clusters/dev.yaml the live secrets filename is clusters/dev.env.
# Live *.env files are Git-ignored. Never put secrets in the YAML file.
#
# Recommended initialization (creates dev.env only if absent):
#   sudo python3 lab/libvirt/create.py --config clusters/dev.yaml --init-secrets
# It generates a key, or adopts the saved key when migrating an existing lab.
# It refuses to overwrite an existing file and does not create any VMs.
#
# Alternatively copy this template manually, replace the placeholder with one
# 32-byte cryptographically random key encoded as 64 hexadecimal characters,
# then set ownership/permissions before create:
#   sudo chown root:root clusters/dev.env
#   sudo chmod 600 clusters/dev.env
#
# This is data, NOT a shell script. Only KEY=value assignments and full-line
# comments are accepted. No export, interpolation, command execution, inline
# comments, multiline values, or unknown variables. Optional paired quotes
# around the hexadecimal value are accepted. Values are never printed.
#
# Keep the same secret across all nodes, retries, and restarts of this cluster.
# Create/destroy never overwrite or delete this file; even destroy preserves it.
# Secret rotation and file deletion are manual user decisions. Changing a key
# for an existing deployment is rejected; runtime identities remain on disk.
ENROLLMENT_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_64_RANDOM_HEXADECIMAL_CHARACTERS
